Index the PowerVR compat layer's per-call lookups.

Every recorded vkCmdBindPipeline, vkCmdBindDescriptorSets, vkCmdPushConstants and
vkCmdPipelineBarrier took a global lock and walked every live command buffer to
find its own, every image barrier walked every image the game ever created, every
push walked the pipeline-layout list and allocated a journal entry, and each call
asked the next layer for its entry point by name. Command buffers, images and
layouts now have hash indexes beside their lists, entry points are cached per
device, and a push or compute bind with the same shape as the previous journal
entry overwrites it in place (replay leaves the same state).

On lavapipe with 64 command buffers, 3000 images and 300 layouts: push 1886 -> 138
ns, bind 334 -> 106 ns, image barrier 10192 -> 202 ns. The upstream BC image probe
prints the same output before and after.

